WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990
- What happens when a
mother and a daughter

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:05.140
set out on a 2000 mile trek
on the Appalachian Trail

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.750
just two weeks before a pandemic hits?

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.730
Well, they keep on trucking,
and they finish that bad boy,

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.800
and here to tell us all
about their amazing journey,

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.540
please welcome Briana and Cambyr Sullivan.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.287
Mothers and daughters!

00:00:18.287 --> 00:00:21.371
(audience applauding)

00:00:21.371 --> 00:00:22.204
Hi guys!

00:00:24.045 --> 00:00:25.470
- Hi, how are you?

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:26.400
- Oh my god, okay.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.550
So you, I have my daughters here today,

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.140
so I love mothers and daughters.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.680
It's like, it's everything.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.790
It's my emotional Achilles
heel from my own past,

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:38.210
and my journey, and destiny here on earth:

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.080
mothers and daughters.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.876
Okay, you traveled 2000 miles
all on your own four feet.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.023
Did you do this?

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:50.670
- Well, we actually, I was
very interested in nature,

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.540
and getting back out
into it and reconnecting,

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.170
and I'd heard about the Appalachian trail,

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.280
but I thought, you know my kids are young.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.760
I won't be able to do
this for quite a while.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.230
And that's where Cambyr became
the catalyst for this year,

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.173
and making it happen.

00:01:05.173 --> 00:01:08.230
- Yeah, about a year before we left,

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:12.970
I was on the internet, and
I found this amazing thing

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.610
called the Appalachian Trail.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:18.210
It was a six month journey,
and a very long walk,

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.490
and I told myself I need to do it.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.697
And so I went into my mom, and I was like,

00:01:22.697 --> 00:01:27.697
"Next year we're doing that," and we did.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:31.230
- Can you talk to my daughters after like

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.170
we finish this segment, Cambyr?

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.003
Thank you.

00:01:34.003 --> 00:01:35.580
Okay. Sorry, go on.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.060
I'm like-

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.950
- I know it was so incredible because

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.410
to prove that she could do this,

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.170
she trained for a half marathon,

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.047
and she worked out all
of the stats and said,

00:01:44.047 --> 00:01:45.127
"We can do this.

00:01:45.127 --> 00:01:47.637
"We can do 13 miles a
day, and we'll finish,

00:01:47.637 --> 00:01:51.117
"if we start March 1st,
and end August 22nd,

00:01:51.117 --> 00:01:52.260
"we can do this."

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.410
And not only did we do that, 13 mile days,

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:58.450
but we ended up having a 48 mile day,

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.680
because it just, it happened.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.770
She was so positive, and
she just made it happen.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:05.603
- Wow.

00:02:05.603 --> 00:02:07.620
Frankie and I took a walk
around our neighborhood today.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.760
I guess that really doesn't compare.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:10.830
(audience laughing)

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:11.663
I mean,

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:15.570
you know, you are so inspiring

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.500
to young ladies out there, really,

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.480
because you know Olive went
to the skate park this weekend

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.640
and you know we're always trying to

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.000
find ways to be physical.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.030
And I mean, this is, you know,
you're a real inspiration.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.330
This is just incredible.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.570
I think you should teach a
TED Talk and a Masterclass

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:36.460
right now, two young ladies out there.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:40.373
What is your advice to try
and try something like this?

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:45.350
- You really have to
know what you're in for.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.800
You really got to understand that

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.950
you will be waking up every day,

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:53.210
you will be walking, and
it might be monotonous,

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:55.960
but you got know that
you can make it through,

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.910
and that you will make it through that.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.560
- Yeah, and I think
having a positive outlook,

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.970
and always keeping a positive mentality,

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:07.300
and thinking a better thought
is really what got us through,

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:11.930
and helped us to maintain
our stamina, and our desire.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:14.890
- I mean, honestly, it is
hard to ask you questions,

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:18.010
'cause my jaw is just
on the table right here.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.530
I'm so inspired by you two.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.736
By the way, I heard you
brought your guitar?

00:03:22.736 --> 00:03:23.937
- I did!

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:26.160
I think that it is super important

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.610
to keep the positivity going,

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.150
and to make sure that you're not bored

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:32.800
from the monotonous routine of just

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.170
getting up and hiking every day

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:35.960
with a big pack on your back.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.880
- And Cambyr, were you into the guitar,

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:42.140
or like a month in where you
like AirPods in and nodding?

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.983
- I loved the guitar.

00:03:43.983 --> 00:03:46.550
I thought it was the most amazing thing.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:48.645
Like so many people just
come up to us and be like

00:03:48.645 --> 00:03:50.606
"Oh my god, is that a guitar?"

00:03:50.606 --> 00:03:54.249
And it was just amazing to
have someone musical as my mom,

00:03:54.249 --> 00:03:56.343
bringing this amazing skill on-trail,

00:03:56.343 --> 00:03:58.346
and it was amazing.

00:03:58.346 --> 00:04:00.242
(audience applauding)

00:04:00.242 --> 00:04:02.210
- As the mother of two daughters,

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.810
I am going to carry you both in my heart,

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:08.350
and try and funnel the
inspiration into our family.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:12.911
Truly, Briana and Cambyr, thank
you so much for being here.

00:04:12.911 --> 00:04:16.911
(inspiring instrumental music)

